[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two small, matte white ceramic bowls placed on a rustic, aged oak wooden table with visible wood grain and small scratches. One bowl is in the sharp foreground, and the second is slightly out of focus in the background, both centered to allow for circular cropping. Camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, clearly displaying the contents. The lighting is soft, natural window light from the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the warm texture of the food. Inside each bowl, a base of thick, creamy, nonfat Greek yogurt is visible. Arranged neatly on top of the yogurt are tender, 1/4-inch thick apple slices that have been baked until they reach a warm, caramelized amber color with subtle golden-brown edges. The apples are coated in a light dusting of cinnamon and nutmeg, with occasional small, dark spice grains visible. A fine drizzle of maple syrup adds a natural sheen to the apple surface. The dish is finished with a rustic scattering of crunchy, toasted chopped pecans over the apples. Props include a small wooden spoon resting casually against the side of the foreground bowl and a few stray pecan fragments and a tiny dusting of cinnamon scattered on the oak surface near the bowls. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene looks like a cozy, home-cooked dessert just finished in the kitchen. Subtle natural imperfections include an asymmetric apple placement and a tiny, realistic drip of yogurt on the bowl's edge. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no text, no watermarks, no hands or faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
]
